description:
Write `D2D1::Matrix3x2F` yourself. A point `(x, y)` is a row vector transformed as `x' = x·m11 + y·m21 + dx`, `y' = x·m12 + y·m22 + dy`:

```cpp
struct Point { float x, y; };
struct Matrix { float m11, m12, m21, m22, dx, dy; };

Matrix identity();
Matrix translation(float x, float y);
Matrix scale(float sx, float sy, Point centre);
Matrix rotation(float degrees, Point centre);       // clockwise on screen (y points down), like Direct2D
Matrix multiply(const Matrix& a, const Matrix& b);  // a * b: first a, then b
Point apply(const Matrix& m, Point p);
bool invert(const Matrix& m, Matrix& out);           // false if not invertible
Matrix zoomAt(const Matrix& view, float factor, Point screenPoint);
```

- `scale` and `rotation` about a centre are: translate the centre to the origin, scale or rotate, translate back.
- `rotation` by `a` degrees about the origin is `m11 = cos a, m12 = sin a, m21 = -sin a, m22 = cos a`.
- `zoomAt`: `view` maps drawing coordinates to the screen. Return a view that is also scaled by `factor` around `screenPoint`, so the drawing point under `screenPoint` stays there.

